# Operator-selected mid-week schedule, America/New_York (2026-11-11).
# Supersedes friday_positioning_schedule.env.example. Apply these keys to the
# existing deployment .env; do not replace it. Trading gates, state path,
# CYCLE_EVERY_WEEKS and CYCLE_ANCHOR_DATE stay as they are — the anchor names
# a WEEK, so moving the weekday keeps the same on/off weeks.
#
# Why. The Friday 17:00 cycle ran after the close: orders are plain DAY market
# orders with no outside-hours flag, so an approved basket waited for Monday's
# open, sized on Friday's close and carried across the weekend. It was moved
# there to follow the Friday positioning release, and positioning rows are no
# longer required of the PM (2026-11-11). Mid-week, in session, an approved
# basket fills the same hour, and a blocked cycle leaves two more sessions
# that week to retry with /cycle.
#
# Everything else is derived from CRON and moves with it:
#   broker readiness check   10:00  (60 min before)
#   committee                09:00  (120 min before)
#   Agent PM decision        10:15  (PM_PRE_CYCLE_LEAD_MINUTES before)
#   cycle + approval card    11:00  New York = 17:00 Warsaw
# AGENTS_COMMITTEE_CRON must be REMOVED from .env (or commented out): it
# overrides the derived time and would leave the committee on Friday 15:35.
CRON=0 11 * * WED
SCHEDULE_TZ=America/New_York
PM_PRE_CYCLE_LEAD_MINUTES=45
